# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# A supervisor program of our own, in place of the PlayChoice-10's BIOS program
# (8T): it lets the watchdog run out, again and again. The real BIOS never does
# (it holds NMI EI high, or DOG DI in its error loops), so without this nothing
# outside the unit tests resets the Z80. The characters and colour PROMs stay
# the real set's (MAME_ROMPATH); only the program is replaced. Lines are
# "ADDRESS: BYTES", hex, after which a "#" starts a comment; everything not
# written reads $FF (an unprogrammed EPROM). Hand-assembled; Z80 cycles in the
# comments where they set a time.
#
# Each boot (power, or the watchdog's reset):
#   - counts itself in 8W ($8800; kept through the Z80's reset) and writes the
#     count to the screen's first character while SDCS is low;
#   - raises SDCS, /PPU RES, /GAME RES, /CNTRL MASK, /SOUND MASK and /DISP MASK
#     (the game starts), then drops /DISP MASK with SDCS high and raises it
#     again (the one-monitor board's flip, once a boot);
#   - on odd boots raises /GAME STOP (the game runs) and holds the watchdog's
#     counter with NMI EI for about 3.5 blanks (one NMI taken, $0066 RETN);
#     on even boots leaves /GAME STOP low (the game stops at its first NMI)
#     and holds the counter with DOG DI instead;
#   - drops the hold and spins: the eighth blank after resets the Z80, whose
#     reset clears both latches, SDCS first, so /DISP MASK falls with SDCS low.
0000: 31 00 88      # LD SP,$8800
0003: 21 00 88      # LD HL,$8800     8W's first byte
0006: 34            # INC (HL)        the boot count
0007: 7E            # LD A,(HL)
0008: 32 00 90      # LD ($9000),A    the screen's first character (SDCS low)
000B: 3E 01         # LD A,1
000D: D3 00         # OUT ($00),A     SDCS high
000F: D3 0A         # OUT ($0A),A     /PPU RES high
0011: D3 04         # OUT ($04),A     /GAME RES high: the 2A03 starts
0013: D3 01         # OUT ($01),A     /CNTRL MASK high
0015: D3 03         # OUT ($03),A     /SOUND MASK high
0017: D3 02         # OUT ($02),A     /DISP MASK high
0019: AF            # XOR A
001A: D3 02         # OUT ($02),A     /DISP MASK low, SDCS high
001C: 3C            # INC A
001D: D3 02         # OUT ($02),A     /DISP MASK high again
001F: CB 46         # BIT 0,(HL)
0021: 28 0C         # JR Z,$002F      even boots
0023: D3 05         # OUT ($05),A     odd: /GAME STOP high
0025: D3 08         # OUT ($08),A     NMI EI high: the counter held
0027: CD 39 00      # CALL $0039
002A: AF            # XOR A
002B: D3 08         # OUT ($08),A     NMI EI low: the counter counts
002D: 18 FE         # JR $
002F: D3 09         # OUT ($09),A     even: DOG DI high: the counter held
0031: CD 39 00      # CALL $0039
0034: AF            # XOR A
0035: D3 09         # OUT ($09),A     DOG DI low: the counter counts
0037: 18 FE         # JR $
0039: 01 28 23      # LD BC,9000      the delay: 9,000 x 26 T-states, 3.5 blanks
003C: 0B            # DEC BC          6
003D: 78            # LD A,B          4
003E: B1            # OR C            4
003F: 20 FB         # JR NZ,$003C     12 taken
0041: C9            # RET
0066: ED 45         # RETN            the blank's NMI, taken once (NMI EI not re-armed)
